<v James Dabbs>I tested a stuntman in a movie set once, and he came out low in testosterone and was terribly unhappy about being low in testosterone. The fact is he still was a stuntman and did all the work that other people couldn't do, so he shouldn't have been focusing upon that testosterone. I think to focus upon the testosterone is the wrong thing to do.
